//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Given an array of N integers, build a Min Heap from the array in place, meaning rearrange the elements of the array so that the array represents a valid Min Heap.

You are also given helper functions parent, left and right that give the parent, left child and right child index of a given index, and a minHeapify function that fixes the heap property at a given index assuming its subtrees are already valid heaps. Use these to build the heap in O(n) time.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example 1
Input
arr = [9,4,7,1,3]

Before

              9
           /     \
          4       7
        /   \
       1     3

Output
[1,3,7,4,9]

After

              1
           /     \
          3       7
        /   \
       4     9

Explanation
Starting from the last internal node and calling minHeapify on each node up to the root produces a valid min heap

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

